# Dev preview on Omarchy

When you need to **build and run the app to test a full GUI preview**, do not launch it on the current coding workspace. Use `bin/build-dev.sh` with `-o` / `--omarchy` so the window opens on a chosen Hyprland workspace (screen).

```bash
bin/build-dev.sh -o 3          # workspace 3 (typical preview screen)
bin/build-dev.sh --omarchy 5   # any workspace N
bin/build-dev.sh -o            # defaults to workspace 3
```

- Prefer asking which workspace to use if the user has not said; otherwise default to `-o 3`.
- Plain `cargo run` / `bin/build-dev.sh` without `-o` is fine for compile-only checks, not for interactive full-app preview on Omarchy.
